@anon.6aa2d360734573fdde4b4ffe4a284ba1.1799 = private unnamed_addr constant [427 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for unnecessary subscript reversal of iterable.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AIt's unnecessary to reverse the order of an iterable when passing it\0Ainto `reversed()`, `set()` or `sorted()` functions as they will change\0Athe order of the elements again.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Asorted(iterable[::-1])\0Aset(iterable[::-1])\0Areversed(iterable[::-1])\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Asorted(iterable)\0Aset(iterable)\0Aiterable\0A```\0A", align 1
