@anon.6aa2d360734573fdde4b4ffe4a284ba1.1854 = private unnamed_addr constant [869 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for functions with a high `McCabe` complexity.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AThe `McCabe` complexity of a function is a measure of the complexity of\0Athe control flow graph of the function. It is calculated by adding\0Aone to the number of decision points in the function. A decision\0Apoint is a place in the code where the program has a choice of two\0Aor more paths to follow.\0A\0AFunctions with a high complexity are hard to understand and maintain.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef foo(a, b, c):\0A    if a:\0A        if b:\0A            if c:\0A                return 1\0A            else:\0A                return 2\0A        else:\0A            return 3\0A    else:\0A        return 4\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adef foo(a, b, c):\0A    if not a:\0A        return 4\0A    if not b:\0A        return 3\0A    if not c:\0A        return 2\0A    return 1\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.mccabe.max-complexity`\0A", align 1
