@anon.6aa2d360734573fdde4b4ffe4a284ba1.1878 = private unnamed_addr constant [845 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for `raise` statements that raise `NotImplemented`.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0A`NotImplemented` is an exception used by binary special methods to indicate\0Athat an operation is not implemented with respect to a particular type.\0A\0A`NotImplemented` should not be raised directly. Instead, raise\0A`NotImplementedError`, which is used to indicate that the method is\0Aabstract or not implemented in the derived class.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aclass Foo:\0A    def bar(self):\0A        raise NotImplemented\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aclass Foo:\0A    def bar(self):\0A        raise NotImplementedError\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `NotImplemented`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/constants.html#NotImplemented)\0A- [Python documentation: `NotImplementedError`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/exceptions.html#NotImplementedError)\0A", align 1
