@anon.6aa2d360734573fdde4b4ffe4a284ba1.1903 = private unnamed_addr constant [691 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of deprecated imports based on the minimum supported\0APython version.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0ADeprecated imports may be removed in future versions of Python, and\0Ashould be replaced with their new equivalents.\0A\0ANote that, in some cases, it may be preferable to continue importing\0Amembers from `typing_extensions` even after they're added to the Python\0Astandard library, as `typing_extensions` can backport bugfixes and\0Aoptimizations from later Python versions. This rule thus avoids flagging\0Aimports from `typing_extensions` in such cases.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Afrom collections import Sequence\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Afrom collections.abc import Sequence\0A```\0A", align 1
