@anon.6aa2d360734573fdde4b4ffe4a284ba1.1940 = private unnamed_addr constant [828 x i8] c"## Removed\0AThere's no [evidence](https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/12754) that generators are\0Ameaningfully faster than list comprehensions when combined with unpacking.\0A\0A## What it does\0AChecks for list comprehensions that are immediately unpacked.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AThere is no reason to use a list comprehension if the result is immediately\0Aunpacked. Instead, use a generator expression, which avoids allocating\0Aan intermediary list.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aa, b, c = [foo(x) for x in items]\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aa, b, c = (foo(x) for x in items)\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: Generator expressions](https://docs.python.org/3/reference/expressions.html#generator-expressions)\0A- [Python documentation: List comprehensions](https://docs.python.org/3/tutorial/datastructures.html#list-comprehensions)\0A", align 1
